====================================================================================================
A. the boson: de Broglie exclusion vs the CMB floor
====================================================================================================
  L* galaxy halo-free needs M_min >= 1e+11 Msun  ->  m <= 5.8e-25 eV
  cluster halo can form needs M_min <= 1e+15 Msun ->  m >= 1.2e-27 eV
  CMB (Planck) floor: m >= 1e-24 eV
  A1 at the L* level alone the gap is only x1.7 -- an EDGE, inside the modelling slop of M_min and of the Planck floor
  massive SPARC discs halo-free (well collects 1e+12 Msun) -> m <= 1.2e-25 eV : gap to the CMB floor x8
  massive SPARC discs halo-free (well collects 1e+13 Msun) -> m <= 2.7e-26 eV : gap to the CMB floor x37
  [PASS] A2 the boson window is EMPTY once the RAR's mass-independence is used: keeping the most massive SPARC discs halo-free needs m <= 1.3e-25 eV, the CMB needs m >= 1e-24 eV -- a gap of >= 7x; fuzzy dark matter cannot be the CMB's dark matter and leave the whole RAR untouched   (gap = x8)

